# Toolchain pin table - the single source of truth for every tool this repo installs or verifies.
#
# Format: one row per line, `<tool> <spec>`.
#   <tool>   the command name the repo calls and a version check runs.
#   <spec>   `<npm-package>@<version>` when npm can install the exact build, otherwise a bare
#            `<version>` naming the minimum accepted, for a tool whose own installer cannot address one.
#   A `<tool>-sha256-<os>-<arch>` row is the sha256 of that tool's extracted binary on that platform.
# A row with `@` after a first character is npm-installable, so the installer installs exactly that build.
# Every floor the repo enforces (bootstrap diagnostics and quota-axi compatibility) derives from
# its row here, so one edit moves installation, detection and the operator-facing diagnostic together.
# Not pinned here, because they are the user's own installs: node, git, gh, tmux, jq, python3, and each harness CLI.
#
# Bump ritual.
# 1. Verify the new version on a real home for one working day, including one dispatch and one merge.
# 2. Change that single row; never edit a row without step 1, and never lower a row.
# 3. Run `bin/jg-test-run.sh tests/jg-one-install.test.sh` and `bash bin/jg-bootstrap.sh`, which must agree
#    with the new row, then ship the row with the verification in the change description.
#
no-mistakes 1.46.0
treehouse 2.0.1
gh-axi gh-axi@0.1.44
chrome-devtools-axi chrome-devtools-axi@0.1.44
quota-axi quota-axi@0.1.67
learn-from-mistakes learn-from-mistakes-axi@0.12.0
done-done done-done-axi@0.6.27
sign-off-axi sign-off-axi@0.7.0
first-draft-axi first-draft-axi@0.3.0
# The message bus every live path in the migration runs on: the JetStream server
# and the client that creates a stream and reads its state. Both ship as release
# archives, not npm packages, so the row is their exact version and
# bin/jg-bootstrap.sh owns the install.
nats-server 2.10.22
nats 0.5.1
# The sidecar and the delivery server the same channel runs on, installed the same way.
daprd 1.19.1
# The workflow engine's timer service, from the same release; it has no version flag, so the installer records the pin beside the binary.
dapr-scheduler 1.19.1
# The policy engine every yes/no rule under policy/ is evaluated by (jg-guard-host.sh eval), a bare release
# binary installed by bin/jg-bootstrap.sh like the rows above.
opa 1.22.0
# Lookout is the only supported fleet dashboard package.
lookout-axi lookout-axi@0.1.0
byokit-accounts @byokit/accounts@0.34.0
takeone-axi takeone-axi@0.4.0
# The table engine's diagram command renders its charts with the WebAssembly build of Graphviz (MIT). No bootstrap check installs it:
# core/machines/bin/chartfit.py stops with this row's install line when the module is missing.
viz @viz-js/viz@3.31.0

# The backlog store: bin/jg-beads.sh runs a binary only when it hashes to these rows, so install.sh and bin/jg-bootstrap.sh read the hash and never start one.
bd 1.3.4
